From f1d565eb23c8a09beb5083d77c9b390d77d54f66 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lucascouts <lucascs@protonmail.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 08:32:31 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] agent_sandbox: a jail receives the vault secrets its project
 chose
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Zeo next §6.53 step 3. 0206 let a vault secret declare the variable a
jail sees and the hosts the value is for; nothing handed it to a jail.

A project now chooses secrets by `secret://` reference in
`agent_sandbox.capabilities.secrets` (a default list, and a per-project
list that replaces it, like `mcp_servers`). At start the launch lists
the vault once, reads each chosen value, and passes three things to
ai-jail:

- `--env NAME` -- the value itself goes only into ai-jail's own
  environment (JailSpawn::env), never onto its command line;
- `--secret NAME=host,host` -- ai-jail gives the jail a placeholder and
  puts the real value only into requests to those hosts, HTTPS
  included, through a CA made for that launch (ai-jail 3.7.1-r1);
- the hosts join the jail's allowlist: the credential is useless
  without them.

Fail closed, because an agent that expects a credential and runs
without it fails later and less clearly, and the wrong credential is
worse than none. The start is refused, with its own sentence in the
nine languages, when:

- the installed ai-jail has only the single-host, plain-HTTP
  `--secret` (the probe reads `KEY=host[,host` in `--help`): its HTTPS
  clients would send the placeholder;
- a chosen reference is malformed, missing from the vault, declares no
  use, cannot be read, or the vault cannot be opened;
- two chosen secrets declare one variable, or a variable the jail
  already sets (HOME, PATH, LANG, XDG_RUNTIME_DIR, ZEO_NO_PROXY) or the
  agent's own settings already forward.

A read failure is logged with the reference and the cause, never the
value; JailSecret's Debug redacts it. The secret list is part of the
settings fingerprint, so changing it asks for a restart.

The settings page's command preview passes no secrets: it has no vault
listing; 0208 shows the choice beside it.

Tests: jail_secrets_tests.rs -- matching, every refusal, the options
and hosts, the options' place before `--` with no value on argv, and
the probe telling the HTTPS-capable `--secret` from the old one.
---

